Packaging qualification checkpoint: 2026-09-28
==============================================

Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

This records development snapshot results, not final release acceptance. See
README.qualification for the commands and acceptance procedure. Results below
cover Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute), amd64, with the dependency backports in the
qore-packagers/qore-testing PPA. They do not qualify other distributions or
architectures. The evidence bundle is qore-production-20260928, retained outside
Git with source/package checksums, dependency inventories and complete logs.

Builds and installed artifacts
-----------------------------

Published snapshot 3.0.0~git20260927.4-0qore1~ubuntu26.04, based on upstream
c58353a24d4baf8699e92c4ab598831e6c442205:

- A fresh unprivileged build of its signed source completed without network
  access, with HOME=/sbuild-nonexistent, full documentation and AOT compilation.
  All 390 core test suites passed; all seven binary packages passed Lintian.
- Published and rebuilt packages passed manifest integrity, ELF hardening and
  AOT metadata checks. Both sets contain 409 runtime ELF files and 389 AOT
  modules. Installed tests cover minimal runtime, the SDK, command-line tools,
  remote debuggers, exact-artifact coinstallation, file verification, purge and
  reinstall. The earlier published .2-to-.4 snapshot upgrade also passed.
- Evidence: rebuild.log, rebuilt-lintian.log, rebuilt-artifacts.json,
  published-artifacts-current.json, rebuilt-lifecycle-fixed/, lifecycle-verified/.

Local snapshot 3.0.0~git20260928.2-0qore1~ubuntu26.04, from 2be76a8aa:

- A fresh offline nodoc build with automatic debug packages enabled passed all
  394 core test suites and binary Lintian. Six regular packages and four debug
  packages were produced. No documentation acceptance is implied by this build.
- All ten artifacts passed inspection. All 410 runtime ELF files have matching
  detached DWARF files, build IDs and debuglink CRCs at the standard debug paths.
- The .4-to-this-snapshot upgrade, four installed autopkgtests, coinstallation
  including debug packages, dpkg file verification, purge and reinstall passed.
  The baseline's qore-doc is removed before the minimal installation test.
- Evidence: nodoc-debug-build/, nodoc-debug-artifacts.json,
  nodoc-debug-lifecycle-complete/.

Subsequent packaging fixes have targeted checks and are not included in those
binary snapshots. The installed CMake export no longer embeds its build/source
directory; installed exports match across different roots, and build-tree
discovery still works through symlinks. An independent UUID module builds from
clean committed sources against the corrected installed SDK and passes 14
tests / 227 assertions. This is SDK qualification, not a UUID package build.
Snapshot changelog generation also passes four regression tests and actual
source-package generation without the previous version-order warning.
The combined packaging and CMake regression suite has 31 passing tests.

Remaining reproducibility work
------------------------------

The published .4 snapshot and its clean rebuild are not fully reproducible.
qore-debug-tools and qore-misc-tools are byte-identical. libqore-dev, libqore20,
qore, qore-stdlib and qore-doc differ. Evidence: rebuild-comparison.json,
rebuild-input-comparison.json and REPRODUCIBILITY.md in the evidence bundle.

Confirmed path-dependent outputs include AOT inline source locations, qpp JSON
source_file metadata, qcc-format.stamp source filenames, and compiler flags
embedded in libqore. The installed CMake export has been fixed separately.
Documentation graph maps/hashes and HTML also differ and still need isolation.
The qore executable's .text section matches; its other differing sections
include build ID and debuglink data. Do not suppress comparison failures.

The compared builds also differ in rust-coreutils version (0.10.0 versus 0.8.0)
and locale declarations. Repeat with exact dependency versions and controlled
environment variations after fixing source-path serialization. A matching
source archive alone does not establish binary reproducibility.

Distribution and module work
----------------------------

The base repository inventory in dependency-matrix.json found:

- Ubuntu 26.04 requires the existing nghttp2, ngtcp2, nghttp3, c-ares and
  tree-sitter backports. ONNX Runtime, Arrow and Parquet are enabled and supplied
  by native distribution packages.
- Debian 13 additionally needs suitable ONNX Runtime and Arrow/Parquet packages.
- Ubuntu 24.04 and 22.04 also lack the required OpenSSL 3.5 baseline; 22.04's
  default LLVM is too old. These need a reviewed dependency and maintenance
  strategy, not just another source upload.

Independent module repositories have been inventoried (36 repositories), but
their Debian packaging has not been created. Package them against the installed
SDK, with their own libraries, resources, licenses, AOT metadata and integration
tests accounted for. JSON, YAML and every module shipped in Qore's modules/ and
qlib/ trees remain part of Qore's packages; do not duplicate them externally.
There are no existing standalone module packages available for upgrade tests.
Migration from source installations needs separate qualification.

Final release gates
-------------------

- Resolve the reproducibility findings, then rebuild and repeat all acceptance
  checks on the exact frozen source version, including the later packaging fixes.
- Qualify the architecture-only build and every advertised distribution and
  architecture; the current evidence is full/nodoc binary builds on amd64.
- Decide and configure debug-symbol publication. The testing PPA had automatic
  debug building/publication disabled at this checkpoint; the successful local
  debug build does not make debug packages available in the PPA.
- Assess ABI compatibility against distributed libqore20 snapshots, qualify
  independent module packages, and test the actual downstream Qorus images.
- Complete license/provenance and dependency security-maintenance review; retain
  signed source and binary manifests and the release qualification evidence.
- Publish only after Qore is ready for release and final acceptance passes.
  This checkpoint does not publish, promote or upload any new packages.
